  "notes": "FORMATION:\n{予|よ} (beforehand) + {告|こく} (announce) → announce beforehand\n\nVERB FORM:\n{予告|よこく}する (to give advance notice, to announce)\n\nRELATED COMPOUNDS:\n- {予告|よこく}{編|へん} (trailer, preview)\n- {次回|じかい}{予告|よこく} (preview of next episode)\n- {予告|よこく}{犯|はん} (crime announced in advance)\n- {予告|よこく}なし (without notice)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {告知|こくち} (notification, announcement)\n- {通知|つうち} (notification)\n- {事前|じぜん}{連絡|れんらく} (advance contact)\n- トレーラー (trailer - loanword)\n\nUSAGE:\n{予告|よこく}なし or {予告|よこく}なしに (without notice/warning) is a common phrase used when something happens unexpectedly or without prior communication.",
